  - Retention policy configuration
```

### Why is change so painful with proliferated topics?

Routing is baked into topic structure, which is the hardest thing to change in a running Kafka estate. If the business adds a fourth size band (extra-large) or a new country (SG), you must create a whole new set of topics, update the producer routing logic, add ACLs, and tell all consumers about the new topics.

At National Bank of India, when the compliance team requested a new "jumbo" transaction size band, the Kafka platform team had to create 200 new topics, update the producer's routing table, add ACLs for three consumer groups, and update the monitoring dashboards. With Solace, it would have been a single new subscription pattern.

```java
package com.bank.kafka;

public class ChangeIsPainful {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("=== Adding 'jumbo' size band to Kafka ===");
        System.out.println("Step 1: Create 200 new topics (3 types x 50 cities x 1 new size)");
        System.out.println("Step 2: Update producer routing table to include 'jumbo'");
        System.out.println("Step 3: Add ACLs for each new topic");
        System.out.println("Step 4: Update all consumer subscriptions");
        System.out.println("Step 5: Add monitoring for 200 new topics");
        System.out.println("Effort: days of platform team work");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("=== Adding 'jumbo' size band to Solace ===");
        System.out.println("Step 1: Publisher starts using txn/IN/Mumbai/savings/jumbo");
        System.out.println("Step 2: Consumer subscribes: txn/IN/*/savings/jumbo");
        System.out.println("Effort: minutes, no broker changes needed");
    }
}
```

