### How do teams mitigate topic proliferation in Kafka?

Teams use three common mitigations, none of which is free.

**Mitigation 1: Coarse topics with consumer-side filtering.** Keep one `bank.transactions` topic and let each consumer filter. Trades topic sprawl for wasted bandwidth and CPU.

**Mitigation 2: Stream processing branching.** Use Kafka Streams or ksqlDB to read the coarse topic and dynamically branch into narrower topics. Centralizes routing but adds a stateful service to operate.

**Mitigation 3: Hybrid approach.** A few high-value slices get their own topics; the long tail is filtered client-side.

```java
package com.bank.kafka;

public class MitigationStrategies {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Mitigation 1: Coarse topic + consumer filtering");
        System.out.println("  Pros: one topic, simple");
        System.out.println("  Cons: every consumer reads everything, wastes bandwidth");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Mitigation 2: Kafka Streams branching");
        System.out.println("  Pros: precise routing, narrow output topics");
        System.out.println("  Cons: extra stateful service to deploy and monitor");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Mitigation 3: Hybrid");
        System.out.println("  Pros: balances precision and simplicity");
        System.out.println("  Cons: some consumers still filter, some topics still created");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("None of these is as clean as Solace wildcard subscriptions.");
    }
}
```

```text
Expected output:
Mitigation 1: Coarse topic + consumer filtering
  Pros: one topic, simple
  Cons: every consumer reads everything, wastes bandwidth

Mitigation 2: Kafka Streams branching
  Pros: precise routing, narrow output topics
