=== Solace: No topic proliferation ===

Publisher uses any topic string:
  txn/IN/Mumbai/savings/large
  txn/IN/Delhi/current/small
  txn/SG/Singapore/savings/jumbo  <- new country + size!

No topics created. No broker changes.

Subscribers just adjust patterns:
  txn/IN/>                  (all India)
  txn/SG/>                  (all Singapore -- new!)
  txn/*/*/savings/jumbo      (all jumbo savings -- new!)

Adding a new dimension value: 0 topics created
Adding a new subscriber: 0 topics created
Total broker objects: unchanged
```

### How do Kafka and Solace compare on topic management?

| Aspect | Kafka | Solace |
|---|---|---|
| Topic creation | Explicit, pre-created per combination | None, topic is a publish-time string |
| Topic count growth | Multiplicative (dimensions product) | Zero growth (one namespace) |
| Adding new dimension value | Create new topics + rewire producers + ACLs | Publisher uses new string, no changes |
| Adding new consumer | Subscribe to existing topic(s) | Register a new wildcard pattern |
| Partition cost | Each topic has partitions (memory, handles) | No partition concept for routing |
| Operational overhead | High: creation, ACLs, monitoring per topic | Low: one namespace, wildcard patterns |
| Change agility | Days (platform team approval) | Minutes (consumer-side change) |

```java
package com.bank.comparison;

public class TopicManagementComparison {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Topic management comparison:");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Kafka: 1800 topics x 6 partitions = 10800 partitions");
        System.out.println("  Creating: platform team approval for each");
        System.out.println("  Changing: days of work for one new dimension value");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Solace: 0 topics to create");
        System.out.println("  Creating: publisher sends any topic string");
        System.out.println("  Changing: consumer adjusts subscription pattern");
    }
}
```

```text
Expected output:
Topic management comparison:

Kafka: 1800 topics x 6 partitions = 10800 partitions
  Creating: platform team approval for each
  Changing: days of work for one new dimension value

Solace: 0 topics to create
  Creating: publisher sends any topic string
  Changing: consumer adjusts subscription pattern
```

### What are common mistakes?

**Wrong: creating hundreds of Kafka topics to match Solace-like routing.**

This leads to operational nightmares: partition explosion, ACL management for every topic, monitoring dashboards that cannot fit on a screen, and days of work every time a dimension changes.

```java
package com.bank.kafka;

public class WrongTopicExplosion {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("WRONG: Creating a topic per routing combination");
        System.out.println("  txn.in.mumbai.savings.large (topic 1 of 1800)");
        System.out.println("  txn.in.mumbai.savings.medium (topic 2 of 1800)");
        System.out.println("  ... 1798 more topics");
        System.out.println("  Result: 10800 partitions, ACL nightmare, brittle routing");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("CORRECT options:");
        System.out.println("  A) Use Solace for fine-grained routing");
        System.out.println("  B) Use one Kafka topic + consumer filtering");
        System.out.println("  C) Use Kafka Streams to branch into a few key topics");
        System.out.println("  D) Hybrid: Solace routes live, Kafka stores durably");
    }
}
```

